<main class="policy-main"><header class="policy-hero"><p>Foodera policies</p><h1>Cancellation and Refund Policy</h1><p class="policy-summary">Clear rules for order changes, cancellation requests, refunds, and support.</p><small>Effective: 26 October 2026 &middot; Version 2026-10-26</small></header><article class="policy-card"><section><h2>1. Before preparation starts</h2><p>You may request a full-order cancellation or removal of one dish while an order is <strong>Placed</strong> or <strong>Confirmed</strong>. Choose one request type, select a reason, and add a note if it helps us review the request.</p></section><section><h2>2. Review and approval</h2><p>A request is not cancelled automatically. Foodera or the restaurant reviews stock, kitchen progress, offer eligibility, and payment status. You will see the decision and related refund status in your order history and notifications.</p></section><section><h2>3. Partial dish cancellations</h2><p>Approved dish removals keep a cancelled item record in your order; they are not deleted from history. The subtotal, applicable offer, and final payable amount may be recalculated. A delivery fee may still apply where delivery remains available.</p></section><section><h2>4. Refunds</h2><p>Cash-on-delivery orders normally do not need a refund. For an eligible online payment, Foodera records a refund request after approval. Refund status is separate from delivery status: <strong>Requested</strong>, <strong>Approved</strong>, <strong>Processing</strong>, <strong>Processed</strong>, <strong>Rejected</strong>, or <strong>Failed</strong>. Any payment-provider processing time is outside Foodera's control.</p></section><section><h2>5. After preparation or delivery</h2><p>Customer self-service cancellation is normally unavailable once preparation begins. Delivered orders cannot be cancelled. If there is a missing item, quality concern, delivery issue, or payment problem, use the support option with the order number so it can be reviewed as an exception or service concern.</p></section><section><h2>6. Offers and pricing</h2><p>If a cancellation makes an order ineligible for a coupon, minimum order value, or targeted offer, the discount may be removed or recalculated before the request is approved. We show the resulting amount in the order record.</p></section><section><h2>7. Help and escalation</h2><p>Keep your order number and any relevant details. Contact Foodera support through the site if you believe a decision, charge, or refund status is incorrect. Nothing in this policy limits rights that cannot be excluded under applicable law.</p></section></article></main>
